// automations.memql
//
// Knowledge-domain lifecycle automations. EMPTY on purpose, and the
// emptiness is the finished state of a migration rather than a gap.
//
// This file used to hold the refresh-cadence cron from Q9 of the
// planner-redesign work: a nightly 02:30 automation firing
// logicRefreshDueKnowledgeDomains, which returned a candidate COUNT and
// did nothing else. memql#644 replaced it with an in-process Go poller,
// integrations/planner/refresh_cron.go, and removed the automation --
// this header kept claiming to house it (memql#4115).
//
// Why Go and not DSL: the elapsed-time check is arithmetic on datetime
// fields, which the MemQL grammar has no form for, and an in-process
// poller cannot depend on the engine's automation scheduler reaching the
// planner node-type binary. The poller runs hourly rather than nightly
// for that reason, with a per-domain "spawned recently" guard so a due
// domain gets exactly one refresh Plan. refresh_cron.go's own header
// carries the full contract.
//
// The other lifecycle duties the earlier header promised -- auto-archive
// of zero-citation domains, supersession rollup -- are unbuilt. They land
// here if they land as automations at all; the split above is the thing to
// weigh first, since anything needing date arithmetic belongs in Go.
